<!--
  PR7/PR8 physics + actuation overlay for the derived MJCF (hand-authored —
  see R-PR7-4 and R-PR8b-*).

  This is the ONLY hand-authored MJCF in the repo. It carries the bits a URDF
  cannot: contact defaults, the head camera sensor site, and the sim-only
  actuation wiring. MuJoCo compiles a base MJCF from the shipped URDF (via
  MjModel.from_xml_path + mj_saveLastXML, see mjcf_model.py) and splices the
  blocks below into it before compiling. A generated MJCF is NEVER checked in —
  the URDF stays the single source of truth (issue #89 / R-PR7-2) and the
  transmissions/ros2_control tags in the URDF are the actuator source of truth
  (R-PR8b-6).

  PR8b probe (issue #92) — dfki-ric/mujoco_ros2_control adaptation (R-PR8b):
  this overlay is now consumed by the dfki-ric sim plugin (not ros-controls).
  Two changes from the ros-controls-era overlay:

    1. Actuator types are what dfki-ric's PRM-based classifier actually
       recognizes (verified against MuJoCo 3.9 PRMs):
         - wheels      -> <velocity kv>   (VELOCITY control; dfki-ric writes the
                                            wheel speed to ctrl). NOT intvelocity,
                                            which dfki-ric mis-classifies as
                                            POSITION.
         - column/arm  -> <position kp>   (POSITION control; dfki-ric writes the
                           driven gripper   position target to ctrl). NO dampratio
                                            — dampratio adds a bias term that
                                            breaks dfki-ric's POSITION pattern
                                            and falls it back to plugin PID.
         - gripper mirrors -> <position kp> (franka hand pattern: BOTH driver and
                                            mirror get their own position actuator;
                                            dfki-ric writes the mirror's ctrl from
                                            the driven command x multiplier).

    2. The 2 gripper <equality> mimics are GONE (neq 2->0). dfki-ric reads the
       URDF <mimic multiplier="-1"> tags natively and drives the mirror joint
       itself in write() by writing the mirror's own actuator command; an
       equality constraint would fight that. nq/nv stay 18; nu is 18.

    3. The head-camera <camera .../> ELEMENT is DELIBERATELY omitted (ncam=0).
       dfki-ric creates a MujocoDepthCamera node for every MJCF <camera>, and
       that node aborts on eglInitialize failure — which is exactly what
       happens on the headless bringup/CI node (no GPU/EGL). The framepos
       sensor on head_camera_site (roadmap #4's RGB-D seam) stays; the
       <camera> is re-introduced when RGB-D is actually driven on GPU-backed
       hardware (roadmap #4). VERIFIED: with the <camera> present the sim node
       dies (exit -6, std::runtime_error 'MujocoDepthCamera: eglInitialize
       failed'); without it the headless sim spawns cleanly.

  Contact defaults and the head-camera framepos sensor + site are otherwise
  unchanged from PR7.
-->
<mujoco>
  <!-- Sane contact defaults (sec R-PR7-4). Tuning is iterative — PR8 / roadmap #4. -->
  <default>
    <geom friction="1.0 0.4 0.02" solref="0.01 1.0" priority="1"/>
  </default>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       Actuators (R-PR8b-6 / R-PR8b probe). Real STS3215 gains + contact/
       friction tuning are roadmap #4; gains here are placeholders that give
       stable PD behavior. Actuator TYPES are chosen to match dfki-ric's
       PRM-based classifier (see header comment) so the plugin drives each
       joint via its own actuator ctrl rather than the fallback PID.
       ====================================================================== -->
  <actuator>
    <!-- mobile base (3 omniwheels): velocity command -> <velocity> actuator.
         dfki-ric classifies <velocity> as VELOCITY and writes the commanded
         wheel speed straight to ctrl. -->
    <velocity name="base_left_wheel" joint="base_left_wheel" kv="10"/>
    <velocity name="base_back_wheel" joint="base_back_wheel" kv="10"/>
    <velocity name="base_right_wheel" joint="base_right_wheel" kv="10"/>
    <!-- column lift: position command -->
    <position name="column_lift" joint="column_lift" kp="100"/>
    <!-- left arm (5 revolute): position command -->
    <position name="left_shoulder_pan" joint="left_shoulder_pan" kp="100"/>
    <position name="left_shoulder_lift" joint="left_shoulder_lift" kp="100"/>
    <position name="left_elbow_flex" joint="left_elbow_flex" kp="100"/>
    <position name="left_wrist_flex" joint="left_wrist_flex" kp="100"/>
    <position name="left_wrist_roll" joint="left_wrist_roll" kp="100"/>
    <!-- right arm (5 revolute): position command -->
    <position name="right_shoulder_pan" joint="right_shoulder_pan" kp="100"/>
    <position name="right_shoulder_lift" joint="right_shoulder_lift" kp="100"/>
    <position name="right_elbow_flex" joint="right_elbow_flex" kp="100"/>
    <position name="right_wrist_flex" joint="right_wrist_flex" kp="100"/>
    <position name="right_wrist_roll" joint="right_wrist_roll" kp="100"/>
    <!-- grippers: 2 driven + 2 mirror jaws, each with its own position
         actuator (franka hand pattern). dfki-ric drives the mirror's ctrl
         from the driven command x -1 (URDF <mimic>). -->
    <position name="left_gripper" joint="left_gripper" kp="100"/>
    <position name="right_gripper" joint="right_gripper" kp="100"/>
    <position name="left_gripper_mirror" joint="left_gripper_mirror" kp="100"/>
    <position name="right_gripper_mirror" joint="right_gripper_mirror" kp="100"/>
  </actuator>

  <sensor>
    <!-- Head camera sensor: a first-class framepos sensor on the camera site,
         plus the site/camera themselves (below). RGB pixel output is
         renderer-based in MuJoCo (no XML RGB <sensor>), so the pinhole
         camera + site here are what roadmap #4's RGB-D render pipeline consumes. -->
    <framepos name="head_camera_pos" objtype="site" objname="head_camera_site"/>
  </sensor>

  <!-- PR7-HEAD-CAMERA-BEGIN
  Head camera sensor site at the REP-103 optical frame, relative to column_top
  (R-PR7-6): column_top -> head_camera_mount (xyz 0 0 0.05, rpy 0) ->
  head_camera_link -> head_camera_optical_joint (xyz 0 0 0, rpy 0 -pi/2 +pi/2) ->
  head_camera_optical_frame. So pos (0,0,0.05), euler (0, -pi/2, +pi/2).
  -->
    <site name="head_camera_site" pos="0 0 0.05" euler="0 -1.5708 1.5708" size="0.01"/>
  <!-- PR7-HEAD-CAMERA-END -->
</mujoco>
